WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.890
Each day of the café is a

2
00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:06.721
list of three numbers.

3
00:00:06.721 --> 00:00:09.268
Monday is twelve, thirty, five

4
00:00:09.268 --> 00:00:10.940
a vector in R three.

5
00:00:11.290 --> 00:00:15.163
Each drink, a column of four numbers

6
00:00:15.163 --> 00:00:17.570
is a vector in R four.

7
00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:20.424
R n is the set of all vectors

8
00:00:20.510 --> 00:00:22.495
with n real components.

9
00:00:22.495 --> 00:00:25.949
Today we draw them in the plane, R two

10
00:00:25.949 --> 00:00:28.107
like the arrow two, one

11
00:00:28.107 --> 00:00:31.560
and look at sets of vectors as a whole.

12
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.174
In R n we can do two things.

13
00:00:35.174 --> 00:00:37.991
Take v equal to one, two

14
00:00:37.991 --> 00:00:40.808
and w equal to zero, one.

15
00:00:40.808 --> 00:00:45.142
Add them, tip to tail: v plus w is one

16
00:00:45.142 --> 00:00:45.900
three.

17
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:51.138
Or scale: minus one times v is minus one

18
00:00:51.138 --> 00:00:52.450
minus two.

19
00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.564
Every linear combination is built

20
00:00:55.648 --> 00:00:57.407
from these two moves

21
00:00:57.407 --> 00:01:00.674
and the result is always in R n again.

22
00:01:00.674 --> 00:01:04.360
You cannot leave R n by adding and scaling.

23
00:01:04.940 --> 00:01:07.525
A subspace is a smaller set

24
00:01:07.621 --> 00:01:09.823
with the same property.

25
00:01:09.823 --> 00:01:11.930
If v and w are in it

26
00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:14.228
then v plus w is in it

27
00:01:14.228 --> 00:01:17.100
and so is any number times v.

28
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.199
Take the number zero

29
00:01:19.199 --> 00:01:21.946
zero times v is the zero vector.

30
00:01:21.946 --> 00:01:25.610
So every subspace contains the zero vector.

31
00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:28.871
Here are three sets in the plane

32
00:01:28.871 --> 00:01:31.077
the line y equals two x

33
00:01:31.077 --> 00:01:33.723
the line y equals x plus one

34
00:01:33.811 --> 00:01:37.163
and the quarter where both coordinates

35
00:01:37.252 --> 00:01:38.840
are at least zero.

36
00:01:38.840 --> 00:01:40.692
Which are subspaces?

37
00:01:40.692 --> 00:01:42.280
Pause and decide.

38
00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:48.726
Only the first, and here is why.

39
00:01:48.816 --> 00:01:51.682
Every point of the line y equals

40
00:01:51.771 --> 00:01:54.637
two x is a multiple of one, two.

41
00:01:54.637 --> 00:01:57.056
Two times it is two, four

42
00:01:57.145 --> 00:01:59.743
minus one and a half times it

43
00:01:59.832 --> 00:02:03.146
is minus one and a half, minus three.

44
00:02:03.146 --> 00:02:06.460
Every combination stays on the line.

45
00:02:06.810 --> 00:02:09.203
In R three the subspaces are

46
00:02:09.288 --> 00:02:11.168
the zero vector alone

47
00:02:11.168 --> 00:02:14.671
the lines and planes through the origin

48
00:02:14.671 --> 00:02:16.380
and R three itself.

49
00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:19.371
Check the plane z equals x plus y.

50
00:02:19.371 --> 00:02:21.678
If two vectors satisfy it

51
00:02:21.678 --> 00:02:23.301
add the equations

52
00:02:23.301 --> 00:02:25.694
their sum satisfies it too.

53
00:02:25.694 --> 00:02:28.856
And a multiple satisfies it as well.

54
00:02:28.856 --> 00:02:30.650
The plane is closed.

55
00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.677
Now three sets in the plane that fail.

56
00:02:34.677 --> 00:02:37.852
The line that passed stays behind

57
00:02:37.852 --> 00:02:39.212
in faint grey.

58
00:02:39.303 --> 00:02:42.296
The line y equals x plus one does

59
00:02:42.387 --> 00:02:44.927
not pass through the origin

60
00:02:44.927 --> 00:02:47.467
so it cannot be a subspace.

61
00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:51.095
Also, zero, one and one, two are on it

62
00:02:51.095 --> 00:02:54.270
but their sum, one, three, is not.

63
00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.884
The quarter plane is closed under adding.

64
00:02:57.884 --> 00:03:00.750
But multiply one, two by minus one

65
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:02.740
and you land outside it.

66
00:03:03.090 --> 00:03:05.383
The two axes together are

67
00:03:05.475 --> 00:03:07.401
closed under scaling.

68
00:03:07.401 --> 00:03:09.694
But one, zero plus zero

69
00:03:09.694 --> 00:03:13.730
one is the point one, one, on neither axis.

70
00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:17.800
A subspace must survive both operations.

71
00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.617
So this belief is wrong

72
00:03:20.617 --> 00:03:23.319
that any line is a subspace.

73
00:03:23.319 --> 00:03:27.420
Here is the line y equals x plus one again.

74
00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:30.424
Only lines through the origin are.

75
00:03:30.424 --> 00:03:32.688
Shift this line down by one

76
00:03:32.688 --> 00:03:34.874
and it passes through zero

77
00:03:34.874 --> 00:03:36.279
now it is closed.

78
00:03:36.357 --> 00:03:38.620
A line that misses the origin

79
00:03:38.699 --> 00:03:40.650
has lost the zero vector.

80
00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:43.861
Here is a test we can run in code.

81
00:03:43.861 --> 00:03:46.337
Pick random members of the set

82
00:03:46.337 --> 00:03:48.659
here the quarter plane: five

83
00:03:48.659 --> 00:03:50.361
three and three, one.

84
00:03:50.361 --> 00:03:52.992
Combine them with random numbers

85
00:03:52.992 --> 00:03:55.081
minus one and minus three

86
00:03:55.158 --> 00:03:57.325
and check whether the result

87
00:03:57.402 --> 00:03:58.950
is still in the set.

88
00:03:59.300 --> 00:04:03.368
The result is minus fourteen, minus six

89
00:04:03.368 --> 00:04:06.928
far outside, down and to the left

90
00:04:06.928 --> 00:04:08.861
the quarter fails.

91
00:04:08.861 --> 00:04:12.827
A plane in R three, z equals x plus y

92
00:04:12.827 --> 00:04:15.980
passed two hundred such tests.

93
00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:20.136
One failure proves a set is not a subspace.

94
00:04:20.136 --> 00:04:22.261
Passing proves nothing.

95
00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:25.890
For the plane, the algebra is the proof.

96
00:04:26.470 --> 00:04:28.992
One subspace matters more than

97
00:04:29.076 --> 00:04:31.178
any other in this course.

98
00:04:31.178 --> 00:04:34.036
Take a matrix A with columns one

99
00:04:34.036 --> 00:04:35.634
two and zero, one.

100
00:04:35.634 --> 00:04:39.081
Send the unit arrows onto these columns

101
00:04:39.165 --> 00:04:42.612
and the grid becomes all the combinations

102
00:04:42.696 --> 00:04:45.470
c times a one plus d times a two.

103
00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:49.507
A sum of two combinations is a combination

104
00:04:49.507 --> 00:04:51.394
and so is a multiple.

105
00:04:51.394 --> 00:04:54.910
So all the combinations form a subspace

106
00:04:54.910 --> 00:04:56.882
the column space of A.

107
00:04:56.882 --> 00:04:59.540
Here it fills the whole plane.

108
00:04:59.890 --> 00:05:00.850
For the café

109
00:05:00.924 --> 00:05:03.362
the column space holds every list

110
00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:05.873
of daily takings that some choice

111
00:05:05.947 --> 00:05:07.720
of prices could produce.

112
00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.010
The next lecture starts there.

113
00:05:10.590 --> 00:05:13.222
Last, a habit for working with AI.

114
00:05:13.299 --> 00:05:16.550
Suppose an assistant says that the vectors

115
00:05:16.628 --> 00:05:19.724
in R three with every component at least

116
00:05:19.801 --> 00:05:21.427
zero form a subspace.

117
00:05:21.427 --> 00:05:24.910
Its slice in our plane is the quarter again.

118
00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:28.104
One counterexample settles it.

119
00:05:28.104 --> 00:05:32.276
One, one, one is in the set, and so is one

120
00:05:32.276 --> 00:05:33.982
one in the slice.

121
00:05:33.982 --> 00:05:37.300
Minus one times either one is not.

122
00:05:37.650 --> 00:05:40.326
The set is closed under adding

123
00:05:40.326 --> 00:05:42.311
but not under scaling.

124
00:05:42.311 --> 00:05:45.850
Test closure before you trust the claim.

125
00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.389
To sum up.

126
00:05:47.389 --> 00:05:51.319
R n holds all vectors with n components.

127
00:05:51.415 --> 00:05:53.907
A subspace is closed under

128
00:05:54.003 --> 00:05:57.837
adding and scaling, so it contains zero.

129
00:05:57.837 --> 00:05:59.850
And to test a claim

130
00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:02.630
look for one counterexample.

131
00:06:02.980 --> 00:06:04.015
Now you try

132
00:06:04.102 --> 00:06:06.862
is the set of vectors with first

133
00:06:06.949 --> 00:06:09.192
component zero a subspace?

134
00:06:09.192 --> 00:06:11.780
And with first component one?

135
00:06:12.130 --> 00:06:13.124
Next lecture

136
00:06:13.124 --> 00:06:15.875
the column space and the nullspace

137
00:06:15.951 --> 00:06:18.550
the two subspaces that decide when

138
00:06:18.626 --> 00:06:20.690
A x equals b can be solved.
